AGPL-3.0-only

This crate is a spike of the `gpu-backend` branch in this fork of the GlobalSim
engine (`race_engine_rs`, upstream `daftuyda/GlobalSim`, pin `paired-draws` at
`00d79fa`).

Engine dependency: `gpu/src/lib.rs` includes the engine's `retail_physics.rs`,
`json.rs`, `replay_frames.rs`, `random_gen.rs` and `retail_random.rs` in place via
`#[path]`, plus `retail_geometry.rs` through a `build.rs`-generated copy with the
module-leading `//!` lines converted to `//` (see `gpu/README.md`, "Geometry
port"), and, under the `initialization` feature, `course_data.rs`,
`retail_sort.rs` and `retail_initialization.rs` via `#[path]`. Those files
remain part of the engine (AGPL-3.0-only, Copyright the
engine's authors); this crate is therefore AGPL-3.0-only as well. The engine's
source is the authority on semantics and is never modified to make GPU code pass
(see `docs/GPU_HANDOFF.md`, "Rules").

The `log10` in `gpu/src/kernels/initialization.cl` is a line-for-line OpenCL
port of the algorithm in the `libm` crate 0.2.16 (`src/math/log10.rs`, MIT OR
Apache-2.0, upstream FreeBSD msun `s_log10.c`), written from the published
source with no file copied.

The restricted tick chain ported here mirrors the Rust oracle
`tools/restricted_oracle.rs` in the JAX port repo `John-UNOwen/GlobalSim-Jax`
(also AGPL-3.0-only), which extracted it from the same engine code; the fixture
it is checked against is that repo's `tests/fixtures/restricted_trace.json`.

`gpu/src/kernels/race.cl` and `gpu/src/kernels/retail_core.cl` are OpenCL
ports written from the engine's `race_solver_retail.rs`, `race_field.rs`,
`race_field_retail.rs`, `race_solver.rs`, `race_solver_builder.rs`,
`conserve_power.rs`, `retail_lane.rs`, `retail_position_keep.rs`,
`retail_states.rs`, `retail_spurt.rs` and `starting_grid.rs`, alongside the
already-listed vendored modules. No engine code is copied into them and no
engine file is modified for them.

No binary artifacts are copied from either repo.
